WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.400
If you’re anything like me,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.560
you have lots of ambitious
plans for the future.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.160
I’ve got a whole series of
new books I want to write,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.400
thousands more
videos to script.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.360
But guess what?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.760
None of us may be able to do
any of the things we want to do

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.240
if we don't have our health.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.480
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.400
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.320
Today we take a look at AMPK,
a fascinating enzyme

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:32.760
that acts as sort of
our body's fuel gauge.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:35.280
In my book on everything
evidence-based in weight loss,

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.080
How Not to Diet, I had a section
entitled "Amping AMPK."

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:44.120
AMPK is an enzyme that acts
as a universal fuel gauge

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.160
for plants and animals,

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:47.480
revving up
when it detects a depletion

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:49.760
of the universal fuel.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:53.600
The universal energy currency
in all of biology

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:56.480
is a molecule called
adenosine triphosphate,

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.880
commonly known as ATP.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.560
The tri in triphosphate means
three, as in tricycle or,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.520
in this case,
ATP's three phosphates

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.720
where energy is stored.

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:09.320
Plants make ATP
with energy from the sun,

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:11.200
and animals make it
by burning fat,

00:01:11.200 --> 00:01:13.160
carbohydrates, and protein.

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.480
The energy is spent
by releasing the phosphates,

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:21.160
which transforms ATP to AMP,
adenosine monophosphate,

00:01:21.160 --> 00:01:22.880
with mono meaning one,

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:25.160
which then can be juiced up
with two more phosphates

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:28.240
back to ATP,
and the cycle continues.

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:30.560
In this way,
every cell in our bodies

00:01:30.560 --> 00:01:32.000
and in every living thing

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.280
is like a little
rechargeable battery.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:38.040
AMP molecules are charged up
with phosphates to ATP

00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:39.400
using sunlight or food

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.480
and then drained back down
to AMP

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.360
to do the cell's work.

00:01:43.360 --> 00:01:45.600
This brings us to AMPK,

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:48.880
or AMP-activated protein kinase.

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.640
A kinase is a type of enzyme.

00:01:51.640 --> 00:01:55.300
What might be the function
of an enzyme activated by AMP?

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:59.000
A buildup of AMP
means the rechargeable battery

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:00.320
is running low.

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:03.760
It's akin to the fuel gauge
in your car reading empty.

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:07.400
As the needle creeps toward
the E, what do you do?

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.120
Add more fuel.

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:12.080
But instead of having
an extra gas can in your trunk,

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.040
you may have junk
in the trunk,

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:15.440
fat stores on your body.

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:17.520
So that's what AMPK does:

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:19.040
It flips the switch
in your body

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.960
from storing fat
to burning fat.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:23.720
That's why AMPK
is not only known

00:02:23.720 --> 00:02:26.520
as the "master energy sensor"
in our body

00:02:26.520 --> 00:02:28.760
but the "fat controller."

00:02:28.760 --> 00:02:31.760
No wonder I featured it
in How Not to Diet.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:34.840
But it can also control aging,

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:36.440
and so also plays
a starring role

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:38.600
in How Not to Age.

00:02:38.600 --> 00:02:40.080
To sustain life,

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.600
each of our cell "batteries"
needs to stay fully charged.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:48.560
This means maintaining a ratio
of about 100 ATP for every AMP.

00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:50.960
So, our body needs
to perfectly balance

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.600
cellular activities
that consume energy

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.520
with cellular processes
that generate energy.

00:02:56.520 --> 00:02:58.000
In times of plenty,

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.600
our cells can plow
full steam ahead.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:02.200
However, in lean times,

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.320
which for animals
means not enough food,

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.680
and for plants
means not enough light

00:03:06.680 --> 00:03:09.160
(darkness is like starvation
for plants),

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.720
AMPK kicks in
to reorient the cell

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.920
into conservation mode

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.840
and start tapping
into our energy stores,

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:17.640
like burning off body fat.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:21.640
Our cells can also institute
a recycling program

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.160
called autophagy.

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.000
Autophagy comes from the Greek
words auto, meaning "self,"

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.080
and phagein meaning "to eat."

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:32.440
So, autophagy literally means
"self-eating."

00:03:32.440 --> 00:03:34.560
It's a housekeeping process

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:36.600
by which defective
cellular components

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.560
like misfolded proteins
that had been allowed

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:41.080
to wastefully build up
in times of surplus

00:03:41.080 --> 00:03:43.840
are broken down and scrapped
for spare parts.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:47.440
This doubles as both salvage
operation and quality control,

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:49.720
scavenging raw materials
in scarce supply,

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:52.000
as well as clearing away
some of the buildup

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.320
of damaged debris
that is implicated

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.280
in the aging process.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:03:57.800
As one review put it,

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:01.680
"The janitor
is the undercover boss."

00:04:01.680 --> 00:04:02.720
This is one of the reasons

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:07.400
AMPK is increasingly recognized
as a pro-longevity factor.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:11.800
AMPK induces autophagy,
which cleans house,

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.440
sweeps away accumulated waste,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:17.240
and effectively institutes
a sort of cellular "reset."

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:19.040
There are three main ways

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.760
longevity researchers
establish an aging pathway:

00:04:22.760 --> 00:04:25.120
Does the factor worsen with age?

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:28.000
If you amplify it,
does it accelerate aging?

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.560
And if you dampen it,
does it slow aging,

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:32.680
and thereby extend lifespan?

00:04:32.680 --> 00:04:36.120
The loss of AMPK activity
as we age

00:04:36.120 --> 00:04:38.880
fits all three criteria.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.920
Our levels of AMPK drop
as we grow older,

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:44.000
and it gets harder to activate.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:46.200
When this decline
is exacerbated,

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.200
aging is hastened (at least
in the hearts of mice).

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.080
And when this process
is reversed,

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:53.680
when AMPK activation
is boosted,

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:56.880
lifespan is extended
in model organisms,

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:58.637
as much as 38 percent

00:04:58.637 --> 00:05:00.960
in a type
of microscopic roundworm

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:03.680
known as C. elegans.

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:06.000
Up and down
the evolutionary tree of life,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.880
one of the most reliable ways
to extend lifespan

00:05:08.880 --> 00:05:11.520
may be long-term
food restriction.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.840
And AMPK activation is thought
to be one of the mechanisms

00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:17.360
for this longevity boost.

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:20.880
What was remarkable about
the AMPK boosting experiments,

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:23.680
though, is that animal lives
can be extended

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:27.360
even though they were allowed
to eat as much as they want.

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:31.040
So, AMPK activators
can effectively fool the body

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:33.160
into thinking it is starving,

00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:36.120
flipping it into
protective housecleaning mode

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:39.680
without having to suffer
the pangs of deprivation.

00:05:39.680 --> 00:05:42.400
AMPK activators
can thereby be considered

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:46.440
calorie restriction mimetics,
or imitators.

00:05:46.440 --> 00:05:50.320
No wonder AMPK is considered
a "druggable" target

00:05:50.320 --> 00:05:52.240
for longevity.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.800
But is there a way we can
naturally boost AMPK activation

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:59.160
to slow aging
without starving ourselves?

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:05.600
The answer is yes,
which we'll explore next.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:08.320
How can we naturally boost
the enzyme AMPK

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.680
to slow aging
without starving ourselves?

00:06:11.680 --> 00:06:15.680
AMPK is activated
by a fuel shortage.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.480
If we don't want to limit
the amount of energy

00:06:17.480 --> 00:06:19.080
going in through our mouths,

00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.960
then we have to ramp up
the amount of energy

00:06:20.960 --> 00:06:23.360
going out through our muscles.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:26.480
Put people on a bike and start
taking muscle biopsies

00:06:26.480 --> 00:06:27.400
while they cycle,

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.560
and you can detect a near
tripling of AMPK activation

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:32.520
within twenty minutes

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:35.200
in both diabetics
and nondiabetics.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:36.800
That makes sense.

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:39.760
The muscles use up
the ATP to contract,

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:43.760
so AMP builds up
and AMPK is activated.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:47.520
That may be one of the ways
exercise leads to weight loss.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:52.760
AMPK activation also leads
to mitochondrial biogenesis,

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:55.760
meaning the formation
of extra mitochondria,

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.840
the power plants
within our cells

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:00.920
where fat is burned
and ATP is created.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:03.520
So, AMPK doesn't
just cause more fat

00:07:03.520 --> 00:07:05.680
to be shoveled
into the furnace,

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.680
it also causes more furnaces
to be built.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:12.280
In this way, AMPK helps explain
why endurance training

00:07:12.280 --> 00:07:15.720
eventually enables us
to run faster and farther.

00:07:15.720 --> 00:07:17.680
So, might an AMPK activator

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:21.080
be like
the fabled exercise-in-a-pill?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.760
Indeed, AMPK activation

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:25.320
can dramatically enhance
performance.

00:07:25.320 --> 00:07:28.640
An AMPK-activator drug given
to sedentary mice for a month

00:07:28.640 --> 00:07:32.120
boosted their running endurance
by 44 percent.

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:34.000
After one such drug
was discovered

00:07:34.000 --> 00:07:35.880
at the famed Tour de France,

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.880
AMPK activators were banned

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:40.240
by the World Anti-Doping Agency.

00:07:40.240 --> 00:07:44.840
So not just fasting in a pill,
but an exercise mimetic too?

00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.320
People are often
"unwilling to perform

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.360
even a minimum
of physical activity..."

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:50.960
wrote a group
of pharmacologists,

00:07:50.960 --> 00:07:53.800
"thus, indicating that drugs
mimicking endurance exercise

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.960
are highly desirable."

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:00.920
The "mass appeal" of such a drug
may tempt "big pharma"

00:08:00.920 --> 00:08:02.920
to view physical inactivity

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:05.960
as a market to be medicalized
for profit."

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.120
But that vision
pales in comparison

00:08:08.120 --> 00:08:12.480
to the universal market
for an anti-aging remedy.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.640
In his essay
"On youth and old age,"

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.800
the Greek philosopher Aristotle

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:21.760
described death
as the loss of inner heat.

00:08:21.760 --> 00:08:24.040
Indeed, the progressive loss
of function

00:08:24.040 --> 00:08:27.240
of the estimated 10 million
billion mitochondria

00:08:27.240 --> 00:08:30.560
spread throughout the body
is considered a core tenet

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:32.120
of the biology of aging,

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:34.200
but mitochondrial dysfunction

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:36.000
isn't just a consequence
of aging,

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.560
but one of its causes.

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:42.200
Dysfunctional mitochondria are
thought to actively contribute

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:43.440
to the aging process,

00:08:43.440 --> 00:08:46.600
an insight illustrated
by a pioneering experiment

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:49.440
published over 30 years ago.

00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:52.040
If you inject mitochondria
from a young animal

00:08:52.040 --> 00:08:54.480
into a human cell,
nothing happens.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.440
The cell doesn't appear
to notice.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:09:00.120
Human skin cells average
about 300 mitochondria each,

00:09:00.120 --> 00:09:02.480
and adding 10 to 15 extras
from a young rat

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:04.560
didn't appear
to have any effect.

00:09:04.560 --> 00:09:08.440
But add the same number
of mitochondria from an old rat,

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:11.920
and the human cells start
showing signs of degeneration

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.800
within just a few days.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:17.000
Even just having a few percent
of those old mitochondria

00:09:17.000 --> 00:09:18.440
was enough to drive
the human cells

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:20.280
to an early grave.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.200
So, age-impaired mitochondria

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.280
don't just become
less efficient,

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:26.720
but may become actively harmful.

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:31.120
So, if centenarian-equivalent
rat mitochondria are so toxic,

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:34.480
how do centenarian
human cells survive?

00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.080
A group of Italian researchers

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:39.800
took some centenarian
skin biopsies to find out.

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.800
Skin samples
taken from the forearms

00:09:41.800 --> 00:09:42.840
of young individuals

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:45.640
were compared to those
of elderly individuals.

00:09:45.640 --> 00:09:49.440
As expected, each mitochondrial
mite from the older cells

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:52.280
was comparatively defective,
less efficient,

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:54.200
leaking free radicals.

00:09:54.200 --> 00:09:55.560
But to the scientists' surprise,

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:58.200
the total amount of ATP
the centenarian cells

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:00.280
were pumping out
was even greater

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.320
than that of the younger cells.

00:10:02.320 --> 00:10:03.920
How is that possible?

00:10:03.920 --> 00:10:07.440
Because of a bulked up
mitochondrial mass.

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.680
It's like if an older Mike Tyson
took on a featherweight.

00:10:10.680 --> 00:10:12.400
Even if pound-for-pound

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:16.360
the whipper-snapper's biceps
were more energy-generating,

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:20.520
Mike's sheer muscular mass
might prevail.

00:10:20.520 --> 00:10:24.320
So how did the centenarian
mitochondria get swole?

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.080
AMPK.

00:10:26.080 --> 00:10:28.400
Mitochondria can take up
anywhere between 2 percent

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.720
and 50 percent
of the volume of a cell

00:10:30.720 --> 00:10:32.520
and are in constant motion,

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:34.320
merging together
and splitting apart

00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.960
like the molten wax
of a lava lamp.

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:38.600
In times of starvation
or stress,

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:41.480
the fusing of individual
mitochondria together

00:10:41.480 --> 00:10:44.720
into a large tubular network
can be advantageous,

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:46.040
in part by diluting
the effects

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:47.480
of damaged mitochondria

00:10:47.480 --> 00:10:50.400
by mixing their contents
in with others.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.840
AMPK appears to accomplish this

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:56.840
by tipping the lava lamp balance
from fission to fusion

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.280
by blocking
one of the proteins

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:00.880
necessary to break mitochondria
back apart.

00:11:00.880 --> 00:11:02.440
This is thought
to be one of the routes

00:11:02.440 --> 00:11:04.120
by which endurance exercise

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:06.560
can rejuvenate
mitochondrial function.

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:08.400
Thanks to AMPK,

00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:11.440
working out may magnify
your mitochondria

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.520
as well as your muscles.

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.600
Our mitochondrial function
does decline with age,

00:11:16.600 --> 00:11:18.880
in part through
the impaired ability of AMPK

00:11:18.880 --> 00:11:20.880
to generate new mitochondria,

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:24.000
but AMPK can build
new cellular power plants,

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:26.840
expand existing ones,
and decommission old ones

00:11:26.840 --> 00:11:28.720
(so-called mitophagy).

00:11:28.720 --> 00:11:32.200
AMPK is said to serve
as a "mitochondrial guardian,"

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.920
and in that role
may help guard against

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:36.720
the ravages
of age-related disease.

00:11:36.720 --> 00:11:39.680
If an AMPK activating drug
really could help us

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:42.200
reap the fat-burning
and health-promoting benefits

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:45.400
of fasting and exercise
without the hunger and sweat,

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:46.920
one could imagine
how it would become

00:11:46.920 --> 00:11:50.560
one of the best-selling drugs
on the planet.

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:53.120
And it is.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:55.960
It's called metformin,

00:11:55.960 --> 00:11:58.280
prescribed more
than 90 million times a year

00:11:58.280 --> 00:12:00.723
in the U.S. alone.

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:04.360
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:07.760
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:12:07.760 --> 00:12:10.680
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:12:10.680 --> 00:12:15.080
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:19.880
If you want to see any graphs, charts,
graphics, images, or studies mentioned here,

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:23.240
